<article class="enc-article">
<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hudhayl ibn Khalaf ibn Razin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 1045</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hudhayl ibn Khalaf ibn Razin was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berber</a> chief of the Banu Razin who made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albarracin">Albarracín</a> independent around 1012, as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">Caliphate</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cordoba">Córdoba</a> broke apart. He ruled the mountainous <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taifa">Taifa</a> of Albarracín until 1045, keeping it independent between the larger taifas of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toledo">Toledo</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zaragoza">Zaragoza</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valencia">Valencia</a>, and founded the dynasty that held it until the Almoravid conquest.</p></div>
